  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${}_{6}{C}_{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ and $r=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{6}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{6!}{(6-3)!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{3!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4}{6} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
